# fixedbugs, defect 570, lane b18-guard, 2026-10-10 (panel 205's R1).
#
# SYMPTOM: `#define my_abs _Pragma("clang diagnostic ignored
# \"-Wsign-conversion\"") my_abs` over `int my_abs(int)`: the probe
# `(void)(my_abs)(a0)` expanded the pragma on its own line, and
# `my_abs(x: u32)` built and printed `5` (panel 205's `callee`).
#
# FIX: every name the compiler writes but a constant's, a function's and
# each releaser, a record's name and tag and each field, is preprocessed as
# the compiler writes it under a file of its own before any unit compiles
# (`cli/pragma_ask.hero`), and a `#pragma` its expansion prints refuses it,
# `ffi_macro_name`, at its declaration: a raise after the name cannot reach
# the line it stands on.

extern "fixedbugs-570-a-macro-naming-the-bound-function-holds-a-pragma.h"
    function my_abs(x: u32) -> i32  #~ ffi_macro_name

function main()
    print(my_abs(5))
